# TypeScript Style Guide

Reference: [Google TypeScript Style Guide](https://google.github.io/styleguide/tsguide.html), [TSDoc](https://tsdoc.org/) ([standard tags](https://tsdoc.org/pages/spec/tag_kinds/)). Linting and formatting: [Tooling](../tooling.mdc).

Follow the Google guide for formatting, typing, naming, imports/exports, and error handling. Below are project-specific rules and additions.

**Out of scope:** React/TSX — [React Style Guide](react.mdc). UI component packages — [React Component Patterns](../integrations/react-component.mdc).

---

## Source file basics

- **File names:** kebab-case (e.g. `query-parser.ts`, `api.ts`, `model.ts`).

## Documentation (TSDoc)

Follow the TSDoc spec for syntax and standard tags. Do not use JSDoc-only tags or syntax.

- Summary in third person, present tense (e.g. "Returns…", "Computes…").
- Document what and when to use; avoid restating the type in the summary.
- Omit TSDoc for trivial getters/setters or when the type is self-explanatory.

## Project-specific

- **Enums:** Prefer **const objects** or **union types** over standard `enum` (better bundle size and tree-shaking).
- **Modern features:** Use **`satisfies`** and **const type parameters** where they improve type safety or inference.
